<title>FINLAND: ASPO SEES IMPROVING EARNINGS IN 1997.</title>
<headline>ASPO SEES IMPROVING EARNINGS IN 1997.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish metals and engineering group Aspoyhtyma Oy said on Thursday it expected full-year 1997 net sales to rise and earnings to improve over last year's 1.1 billion markka sales and 65.5 million markka before extras and tax.</p>
<p>&quot;The group's net sales for the entire year are expected to rise and its earnings are expected to improve over last year,&quot; Aspo said in its January-April interim report.</p>
<p>Aspo's four-month profit rose to 33.6 million markka from 7.8 million in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
